# Response headers, applied by Cloudflare Workers Assets.
#
# Cloudflare CONSUMES this file rather than serving it, so it never appears as
# a route. It lives in public/ because that is what gets copied into dist/,
# which is the assets directory wrangler.jsonc points at.
#
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE
#
#   Strict-Transport-Security   set at Cloudflare (SSL/TLS -> Edge Certificates
#                               -> HSTS). It is emitted at the edge on every
#                               response including redirects, which this file
#                               cannot reach. One owner; the edge is the better
#                               one.
#   X-Content-Type-Options      set at Cloudflare too, by the "No-Sniff Header"
#                               toggle inside that same HSTS dialog.
#
# Do not add either here as well. Two sources would mean two copies of the same
# header on every response, and the next person to read this file would have no
# way to tell which one was authoritative.
#
#   Content-Security-Policy     not set, deliberately. The CloseBot widget
#                               injects its own stylesheet and sets `background`
#                               inline at runtime, so script-src/style-src would
#                               need 'unsafe-inline' to keep it working, which
#                               gives up most of what a CSP buys. Revisit if the
#                               widget ever gains real theming support -- see
#                               the note in src/styles/closebot-widget.css.

/*
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
